    <h1>Uptime Kuma Alternative — No Server, No Docker Required</h1>

    <div class="quick-answer">
      <p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> PingWatch is a fully hosted alternative to Uptime Kuma. You do not need a server, a VPS, or Docker. Sign up, add your URL, and monitoring starts in under 2 minutes. Alerts go to Telegram, Discord, Slack, or Email — with the reason for the outage included.</p>
    </div>

    <p>Uptime Kuma is a popular open-source uptime monitor — but it requires you to host it yourself. That means setting up a VPS, installing Docker, keeping the app updated, and making sure the monitoring server itself stays online. For many developers, that is more overhead than the monitoring is worth.</p>

    <p>PingWatch removes all of that. There is nothing to install, nothing to maintain, and no server to manage. You get the same core functionality — automated checks, downtime alerts, recovery notifications — without the infrastructure work.</p>

